WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.770
Choose a place where resting is safe.

2
00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:07.530
You may lie down, recline, or sit with the back, head, and feet supported.

3
00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:13.060
Adjust anything that would make the body work unnecessarily.

4
00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.850
Keep your eyes open if that feels steadier.

5
00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:21.350
This is not a practice for staying alert during an activity.

6
00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:26.220
There is nothing to achieve, and sleep is not the goal.

7
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.310
If sleep comes, that is not a mistake.

8
00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:34.670
If you remain awake, nothing has gone wrong.

9
00:00:42.472 --> 00:00:44.302
Notice the room before turning inward.

10
00:00:46.002 --> 00:00:50.232
Take in the direction of light, the nearest sound, and the surface beneath you.

11
00:00:51.932 --> 00:00:53.932
Let the room remain part of the practice.

12
00:00:55.632 --> 00:00:59.212
You can open your eyes, move, or stop whenever you choose.

13
00:01:12.216 --> 00:01:14.116
Feel the broad outline of the body.

14
00:01:15.816 --> 00:01:17.106
The places touching support.

15
00:01:18.806 --> 00:01:21.126
The places surrounded by air or fabric.

16
00:01:22.826 --> 00:01:26.726
You do not need to scan every detail.

17
00:01:28.426 --> 00:01:30.206
Let the whole shape be here at once.

18
00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:49.130
Notice where the surface receives your weight most clearly.

19
00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:55.700
Perhaps the back of the head, shoulders, back, pelvis, legs, or feet.

20
00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:58.870
There is no need to press down.

21
00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:04.410
Let gravity and the surface meet each other without your help.

22
00:02:23.915 --> 00:02:26.875
The body may still be holding itself in small ways.

23
00:02:28.575 --> 00:02:29.355
That is allowed.

24
00:02:31.055 --> 00:02:33.485
Rest does not require perfect release.

25
00:02:35.185 --> 00:02:41.225
Simply notice one place that is working: the forehead, tongue, fingers, belly, or toes.

26
00:02:42.925 --> 00:02:46.125
Ask whether five percent less effort is available.

27
00:02:47.825 --> 00:02:50.125
If not, let it be exactly as it is.

28
00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:11.030
Bring attention to the eyes.

29
00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:16.530
They may be closed, softly focused, or looking at one steady point.

30
00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:21.430
Feel the small muscles around them without demanding softness.

31
00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:26.120
Let seeing or not seeing take very little work.

32
00:03:42.375 --> 00:03:44.055
Notice the jaw and mouth.

33
00:03:45.755 --> 00:03:49.205
The teeth can remain apart if that is comfortable.

34
00:03:50.905 --> 00:03:53.335
The tongue can rest wherever it naturally lands.

35
00:03:55.035 --> 00:03:57.145
Swallow or adjust when you need to.

36
00:03:58.845 --> 00:04:00.255
Nothing has to become loose.

37
00:04:16.509 --> 00:04:18.449
Feel the shoulders and arms.

38
00:04:20.149 --> 00:04:24.689
Sense their weight traveling through elbows, forearms, wrists, and hands.

39
00:04:26.389 --> 00:04:30.119
Imagine that the surface is willing to hold the full weight of each arm.

40
00:04:31.819 --> 00:04:35.589
You do not have to make the arms heavy; just notice how much is already being carried.

41
00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:56.664
Let the hands be unoccupied.

42
00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:02.504
Fingers may curl, open, touch one another, or rest on clothing.

43
00:05:04.204 --> 00:05:07.554
Notice temperature in the palms and the quiet shape of the hands.

44
00:05:09.254 --> 00:05:13.514
For these moments, they do not need to hold, reach, type, or prepare.

45
00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:35.160
Bring attention to the back of the body.

46
00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:40.930
Feel the areas of clear contact and the small spaces where the body curves away from support.

47
00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:44.380
Let both contact and space belong.

48
00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:50.080
If discomfort asks for a change, move slowly and arrange the support again.

49
00:06:12.836 --> 00:06:14.526
Notice the front of the body breathing.

50
00:06:16.226 --> 00:06:20.686
There may be movement in the chest, ribs, belly, or somewhere less obvious.

51
00:06:22.386 --> 00:06:23.266
Do not deepen the breath.

52
00:06:24.966 --> 00:06:29.446
Let each inhale arrive in its own size, and let each exhale finish without being pushed.

53
00:06:52.202 --> 00:06:55.792
For three breaths, notice only the moment when effort changes.

54
00:06:57.492 --> 00:06:59.272
The inhale may gather a little energy.

55
00:07:00.972 --> 00:07:03.992
The exhale may release some, or may simply be an exhale.

56
00:07:05.692 --> 00:07:07.772
No response is required.

57
00:07:30.528 --> 00:07:32.108
Feel the pelvis and legs.

58
00:07:33.808 --> 00:07:36.138
Notice their broad weight and the way it is distributed.

59
00:07:37.838 --> 00:07:39.708
One side may feel different from the other.

60
00:07:41.408 --> 00:07:46.808
Let the thighs, knees, lower legs, and feet be supported without needing symmetry.

61
00:08:09.564 --> 00:08:11.104
Bring attention to the feet.

62
00:08:12.804 --> 00:08:18.114
Feel heels, soles, toes, socks, bedding, floor, or air.

63
00:08:19.814 --> 00:08:22.184
The feet have no next place to reach during this practice.

64
00:08:23.884 --> 00:08:24.894
They can remain here.

65
00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:47.270
Now sense the body from head to feet as one resting shape.

66
00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:50.750
Some areas may feel settled.

67
00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:57.530
Others may be restless, alert, numb, uncomfortable, or unclear.

68
00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:00.820
Deep rest can include all of that.

69
00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:05.630
You are not waiting for a special state before rest is allowed.

70
00:09:31.637 --> 00:09:32.897
Thoughts may continue.

71
00:09:34.597 --> 00:09:39.357
Plans, fragments, images, and unfinished conversations may appear.

72
00:09:41.057 --> 00:09:42.747
You do not need to empty the mind.

73
00:09:44.447 --> 00:09:50.837
When you notice a thought, let it be one small event inside a larger field that also contains weight, sound, temperature, and breath.

74
00:10:16.844 --> 00:10:19.864
Listen to the nearest sound, then a sound farther away.

75
00:10:21.564 --> 00:10:24.164
Let hearing happen without following the story of the sound.

76
00:10:25.864 --> 00:10:28.044
Notice the quiet that surrounds or follows it.

77
00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:52.910
Return to the feeling of being held.

78
00:10:54.610 --> 00:10:57.240
The surface does not ask whether you are resting well.

79
00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:00.820
It receives the weight that is here.

80
00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:06.280
Let the next exhale end, and wait without hurry for the next inhale.

81
00:11:35.538 --> 00:11:38.738
If wakefulness is strong, it does not need to be defeated.

82
00:11:40.438 --> 00:11:48.408
Feel wakefulness as energy in the body: brightness behind the eyes, movement in the chest, active thoughts, or an urge to shift.

83
00:11:50.108 --> 00:11:52.728
Give that energy room while the body remains supported.

84
00:12:15.484 --> 00:12:18.964
If drowsiness is present, you do not need to hold on to the instructions.

85
00:12:20.664 --> 00:12:22.194
Sounds may move to the background.

86
00:12:23.894 --> 00:12:28.234
If you lose the thread and return later, begin again with one point of contact.

87
00:12:29.934 --> 00:12:31.044
Nothing was missed.

88
00:13:00.302 --> 00:13:02.952
For a little while, release the task of following.

89
00:13:04.652 --> 00:13:08.852
Let sound, breath, and sensation come and go without arranging them.

90
00:13:47.862 --> 00:13:49.442
Begin to notice the room again.

91
00:13:51.142 --> 00:13:53.522
Light, temperature, and sounds.

92
00:13:55.222 --> 00:13:58.242
Feel the outline of the body and the places where it meets support.

93
00:13:59.942 --> 00:14:02.612
There is no need to decide whether the practice worked.

94
00:14:18.866 --> 00:14:22.426
If you are continuing to rest, you may let the guidance end here.

95
00:14:24.126 --> 00:14:27.086
If you are getting up, invite movement into fingers and toes.

96
00:14:28.786 --> 00:14:31.296
Bend or stretch only as your body prefers.

97
00:14:32.996 --> 00:14:38.116
Roll or sit slowly enough to remain oriented, pausing before you stand.

98
00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:54.380
Rest did not require sleep, stillness, or a blank mind.

99
00:14:56.080 --> 00:15:00.000
For these minutes, the body was allowed to be supported without having to produce a result.
